      <image:loc>https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5b893719c258b4ea14935cd9/1583161676424-707OW6O6H5WJUJKQRMYV/image-asset.jpeg</image:loc>
      <image:title>My Science - Experiment</image:title>
      <image:caption>Design microcosms to mimic the mathematical equations and look for places where experimental results are disagreeing with theory or where I can show contrasts between competing candidate mechanisms.</image:caption>
    </image:image>
    <image:image>
      <image:loc>https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5b893719c258b4ea14935cd9/1583161717544-KJ6YAXIZWNIOM8I4NRO5/image-asset.jpeg</image:loc>
      <image:title>My Science - Theory</image:title>
      <image:caption>Finding mathematical tools that are able to mechanistically describe the way emergent properties form in nature. I have a fondness for geometry, which plays nicely with the math of Einstein’s theory of relativity.</image:caption>
    </image:image>
    <image:image>
      <image:loc>https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5b893719c258b4ea14935cd9/1583161656949-OGPF1JOGXQ0009UK8U01/image-asset.jpeg</image:loc>
      <image:title>My Science - Simulation</image:title>
      <image:caption>Explore the universe of outcomes possible from the simple set of rules laid out in the theory. Watching models behave under many different conditions points me to the best situations for drawing experimental contrasts.</image:caption>
    </image:image>
